{"c":[{"id":"37e4af8adcf8abcf","sum":"C1-H12: WARNS-word sentences go whole; page plans end with a row:true hand-off; Asks read the tab left only at fill/pagePlan; host.sock in <home>/sockets (CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full); .fixedSize(horizontal:) clips wraps; no lockf build.lock in with-heavy.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"cd14b8843dd9d3ee","sum":"C1-I6: a WARNS-word sentence goes whole or not at all; page plans end with a row:true hand-off (no executor step); an Ask reads the tab left only at its fill step or pagePlan; ambient fill leaves a goal's page alone; the hourly budget holds pageWalked.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2691af9702ea9f68","sum":"C1-I6: a value whose sentence holds a WARNS word goes with it as a required clause or not at all; page plans end with a row:true hand-off step ('You press <label>' / 'The rest is yours') with no executor step, so seg.plan.steps is one shorter.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T032641Z-df47ef2e50ca5a79","text":"C1: a value whose own sentence holds a WARNS word goes with that sentence as a required clause or not at all; sentence ends are conservative (lowercase word or digit before, capital after). Whole-line clauses cost corpus clinic-intake two values.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T062218Z-bb39f9f0467bc5ce","text":"I6: page plans end with a GoalStep row:true (kind handoff, 'You press <label>' or 'The rest is yours'); it is always the last step, lower.ts gives it no executor step, so seg.plan.steps is one shorter than seg.steps.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"740e3d49bc3a2762","sum":"I6: an Ask reads the tab left only at planAsk's fill step or pagePlan (owner: offer key or goal id); ambient fill leaves a goal's page alone (goalOnPage); the hourly budget (balanced 4) holds pageWalked, so the load journey lifts offersPerHour.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T062227Z-47ccc650cd567ff8","text":"I6: an Ask's tab read happens only at planAsk's fill step (fillModel) or in pagePlan; owners are the offer key or goal id; ambient fill/ready-on-load leave a page with a planning/awaiting/running goal alone (goalOnPage) and TabSource refuses an ambient read over a pinned goal.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T062227Z-6c026cce4f5fd842","text":"I6: page-loop-eval runs every page in one helper; the hourly offer budget (balanced 4) holds pageWalked before the ready-on-load check, so the load journey lifts offersPerHour; fill.load_held_<rule> counts holds.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c154314373edc26c","sum":"H11-H12: host.sock in <home>/sockets, release answers state+spend unless CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full; route page-engine test apply to its own helper; .fixedSize(horizontal:) clips wrapped panels (exact width); never lockf build.lock inside with-heavy.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5e0b1d7fe48d167f","sum":"H12-I6: host.sock is <home>/sockets/host.sock; release builds answer only state and spend unless CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full (harnesses setenv it); onboarding auto only without --home/--settings; helper page-engine tests route apply to their own helper.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T035452Z-68fb99dd307065d5","text":"H12: host.sock moved to <home>/sockets/host.sock (default CaretV2/sockets); release builds answer only state (allowlist) and spend unless CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full, so release-build harnesses must setenv it. Onboarding defaults to auto only without --home/--settings.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T062227Z-7e02cffa1979776c","text":"I6: helper tests with a page engine must route its apply to their own helper (capture it in a local); a shared 'helper' variable lets an earlier test's trailing walk land in the next test's model.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"86a6db3d2adf8e6a","sum":"H11: under .fixedSize(horizontal: true) wrapped text measures as one line and panels clip: use an exact .frame(width:) with vertical fixedSize; build.lock is a symlink to heavy.lock, so lockf build.lock inside with-heavy deadlocks.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T063851Z-1e89e23b19f1384e","text":"H11: a SwiftUI view under .fixedSize(horizontal: true) is measured at its ideal width, so wrapped text counts as one line and the panel clips its top and bottom; give it an exact .frame(width:) and fixedSize(vertical) only (PopupView PopupWidth).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T063851Z-3a51e09ec56311ba","text":"H11: ~/.caret-run/locks/build.lock is a symlink to ~/.long-run/locks/heavy.lock; wrapping lockf build.lock inside with-heavy.sh (which holds heavy.lock) deadlocks while holding the heavy lease.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1ef09e53bf12acfa","sum":"J1-H13: Jev confidence (p_max-1/n)/(1-1/n); daily cap throws JevCapError; replay cache fixture-only; no distilling Jev output; test pageFields via the host debug socket; page inline offers are OfferSource.page; launchd argv0 is relative.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d174639a9c85f705","sum":"J1: Jev confidence is (p_max - 1/n)/(1 - 1/n); a daily spend cap (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP $0.50) throws JevCapError; the replay cache takes fixture text only; TypeSafe's MCA s2.3(b) forbids distilling Jev output.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"987e4b1534648136","sum":"J1: Jev confidence is (p_max - 1/n)/(1 - 1/n) over n options (not the top-two margin judge.ts says; equal only for n=2); makeJevClient holds a per-day spend cap (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP, default $0.50) and throws JevCapError; vitest uses a temp spend dir.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T065440Z-6320f5713756d4a4","text":"J1: TypeSafe documents Jev's Choice confidence as (p_max - 1/n)/(1 - 1/n) over n options (docs.typesafe.ai/confidence), not the top-two margin routing/judge.ts describes; the two agree only for two options. engines/decide/confidence.ts computes other engines' confidence this way.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T065544Z-2b923d2a58b8f2cf","text":"J1: makeJevClient holds every request against a per-day spend file (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP, default $0.50; CARET_JEV_SPEND_DIR) and throws JevCapError (kind cap) past it; vitest.config.ts points the spend dir at a temp dir.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0d659675b89b1bba","sum":"J1: the replay cache and --log-requests take only fixture text (harness lists fixture window ids; the helper refuses the cache); TypeSafe's MCA s2.3(b) forbids distilling Jev output: train local models on Caret's answer keys or a permissive teacher.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T065553Z-29f2d5c421092ef7","text":"J1: the replay cache (engines/decide/cache.ts) and --log-requests take only fixture text: a harness lists its fixture window ids and says if its memory and plan text (window id 'plan') are fixtures; charged windows are checked too. The helper refuses CARET_JEV_CACHE.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T065553Z-310f47ee41817c11","text":"J1: TypeSafe's Master Customer Agreement s2.3(b) (2026-09-23) forbids using Jev's Output for distillation or to train an imitating model; train a local model on Caret's answer keys or a permissive teacher instead.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1e39825f89d0ff0d","sum":"H12-H13: inject a test pageField via the host debug socket (the bundled helper gets allowlisted env only); page inline offers are OfferSource.page and Tab sends pageInsert; a note window needs its own app in helper tests; launchd's argv0 is relative.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"379ec0af76ae5f62","sum":"H13: the bundled helper gets only allowlisted env (ServiceLauncher), so inject a test pageField via the host debug socket; page inline offers are OfferSource.page (native ghost clears skip them), insertsText false, and Tab sends pageInsert.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T080508Z-2110f7480275cbcf","text":"H13: the bundled helper gets only allowlisted env (ServiceLauncher: HOME, USER, LANG, TYPESAFE_API_KEY, CARET_ENV_FILE...), so a helper-side test switch never reaches it from Caret.app; inject a pageField through the host debug socket instead.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T080508Z-bc4a09143ef1ff5b","text":"H13: page inline offers use OfferSource.page (never .engine), so HostCoordinator's ghost clears on AX focus changes leave them alone; Claim.insertsText is false for a page ghost and PageInlineMachine sends pageInsert.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"940d166167db3d8d","sum":"H12-H13: launchd starts the agent with relative argv0 'Contents/MacOS/Caret' (use launchctl print's pid or lsof); in helper tests a non-page window with the browser's pid is passed over as Chrome's toolbar, so give a note window its own app.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T080508Z-ed6af011d8df3dcf","text":"H13: in helper tests, a non-page window sharing the page's browser pid is passed over as Chrome's toolbar (H10 ScreenModel.windowBefore); give a note window its own app (NOTES_APP) or TabSource reads the wrong tab.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T082217Z-6e9f887494c1affe","text":"H12: launchd starts the SMAppService agent as relative argv0 'Contents/MacOS/Caret', so pgrep/ps matching on /Applications/Caret.app misses the host; use launchctl print's pid or lsof txt. A fresh VM guest makes no helper Jev request (no transfers), fill or first look.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
